---
/**
 * The section that must not be softened. It sits outside the `Section`
 * rhythm on purpose: a warning that looks like every other card reads as
 * marketing, and this one is the honest limit of the current release.
 */
---

<section id="security" class="defer-offscreen-rendering border-border-subtle border-t px-6 py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <div
      class="animate-fade-in-up opacity-0-initial border-warning/35 bg-warning/[0.04] rounded-xl border p-7 sm:p-9"
    >
      <p class="text-label-md text-warning font-mono uppercase">What you are agreeing to</p>

      <h2 class="text-headline-md mt-3">
        An agent you connect can run anything inside that project.
      </h2>

      <div class="text-body-lg text-foreground-muted mt-5 space-y-4">
        <p>
          Paths are confined to the project root, and that confinement is the single security
          control in this release. Commands are <strong class="text-foreground">not filtered</strong
          >, and there is no approval step: <code class="text-foreground font-mono">run_command</code
          > will run what it is given, inside that directory, on whichever machine is serving it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Connect projects you are comfortable letting an agent change. Revoking a machine from the
          dashboard closes its connection immediately, so that is the stop button.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-body-md text-foreground-faint border-warning/20 mt-6 border-t pt-5">
        Remote approvals are the next thing to build. MCP 2026-07-28 standardised the mechanism
        (<code class="font-mono">inputRequired</code>) and it is already available in the SDK, so
        this limit is a matter of scope rather than one of design.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
